+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                 |
+| ------ | --------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37  |
+| Status | Draft                 |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` currently forwards any input directly to the executor without checking it against the tool's declared `inputSchema`. This spec describes the validation behaviour that closes that gap: the registry validates input before the executor runs, returns a `ToolResponse` on failure rather than throwing, and compiles static schemas at registration time so a broken schema is caught at startup.
+
+## Validation Contract
+
+- When `execute` receives input that fails the tool's `inputSchema` validation, it returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing or invalid field, and the executor is not invoked ([validated by: rejects missing required field: returns ToolResponse naming the field, executor not invoked](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+
+- When `execute` receives input that passes schema validation and contains extra properties not declared in the schema, those extra properties are forwarded to the executor without modification. `additionalProperties: false` is never injected; default values are never coerced; the executor sees exactly what the model sent.
+
+- When a field in the input has the wrong type, the rejection `result` names the field path and expected type but does not include the field's value. Tool input is where identifying data enters the engine and the engine redacts nothing today; the validation message must not leak it ([validated by: rejects wrong type: message names the field path, does not contain the offending value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L25)).
+
+- `register` compiles a static tool's `inputSchema` immediately; a schema that cannot be compiled causes `register` to throw rather than waiting until `execute` is called, and the thrown message names the tool so the error is actionable at startup ([validated by: throws at registration time for an uncompilable schema, message names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L44)).
+
+## Orchestrator Integration
+
+A schema rejection is a `ToolResponse`, not a thrown exception. The orchestrator's `Promise.all` over tool calls propagates a throw out of the processing loop, fires `onError`, and reaches the WebSocket error handler before a `StreamEndMessage` can be sent. Returning a `ToolResponse` instead keeps the rejection inside the existing tool-result message flow and within the `DEFAULT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS` budget.
+
+- When a tool call with invalid input passes through `createChatOrchestrator`, `processMessage` resolves rather than throws, and the rejection text appears in the tool-result message the provider receives on the following round so the model can correct the call ([validated by: processMessage resolves and rejection text is visible to provider on the retry round](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L18)).
